  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Saturday)\nIssued at 1240 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nRidge of high pressure remains expected to expand eastward into\nthe southern Plains Sunday into the first half of the upcoming\nweek. At the same time, southerly low level flow and weak low\nlevel moisture advection look to continue across the CWA. These \nconditions will help to keep the heat and humidity going into at\nleast the first half of next week. High temperatures each day in\nthe mid 90s to around 103 deg are forecast. Slightly more breezy \nwinds could mix out dewpoints a little better each afternoon \nSunday to Tuesday, though heat index values in the 100 to 109 deg \nrange are still anticipated for much of the CWA. For now have \nissued a Heat Advisory for much of eastern Oklahoma and also the \nArkansas River valley of west central Arkansas Sunday afternoon. \nDepending on how dewpoints play out, the advisory could be \nexpanded to cover more of northeast Oklahoma.\n\nIndications continue to hint at the potential for the ridge to sag\nsouth/southeast during the second half of next week, though much\nuncertainty remains among extended model/ensemble solutions. As \nof this forecast, the greater potential for a boundary to approach\nthe region could be late week into next weekend. Will continue \nwith low chance PoPs across the northern part of the CWA. However,\nif the boundary gets held up north of the CWA, then hot/humid \nconditions could remain ongoing. Will just have to wait and see...",
